hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"258","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said: ¤ ¤ ""By Allah, I seek the forgiveness of Allah, and repent to Him more than seventy times in a day."
"259","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said: ¤ ¤ ""O people, repent to Allah, for I verily repent to Him one hundred times a day."
"260","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said: ¤ ¤ Whoever says: ¤ ¤ Astaghfirullāha ‘l-'Aẓīm alladhi lā ilāha illā huwa ‘l-ḥayyul-Qayyūm wa atūbu ilayh. ¤ ¤ Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said: Whoever says: ¤ ¤ I seek the forgiveness of Allah the Mighty, Whom there is none worthy of worship except Him, the Living, the Eternal, and I repent to Him, Allah will forgive him even if he has deserted the army's ranks."
"261","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said: ¤ ¤ ""The closest that the Lord comes to the slave is in the last portion of the night. So, if you are able to be among those who remember Allah in this hour, then be among them."
"262","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said: ¤ ¤ ""The closest that the slave comes to his Lord is when he is prostrating, so invoke Allah much (in prostration)."
"263","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said: ¤ ¤ ""It is a heavy thing for my heart if I do not seek Allah's forgiveness a hundred times a day."
